From 203777a1ffe1a91f822ae52f79830edc16b828d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:12:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: aspeed: Add AST2700 UART routing support

Add the AST2700 Node 0 and Node 1 UART-routing selector tables to the
Aspeed UART-routing driver. The new compatible strings expose the valid
UART-to-I/O routing choices through the existing sysfs interface.

Ported aspeed-uart-routing.c from:
https://github.com/AspeedTech-BMC/linux/commit/a8a45837ebdb62ab92d7760f7f4eed8c5ffec974
Upstreaming in process:
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-aspeed/20260203-upstream_uart_routing-v1-2-6bd5dd75ee3b@aspeedtech.com/

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
---
 drivers/soc/aspeed/aspeed-uart-routing.c | 425 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 424 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

